                                text "Validation sweep regenerated on the current toolchain and covering all eight workloads; the gate test now checks the artifact for every one, and scripts/check-performance.sh exits 0. Regeneration was necessary for two independent reasons, not one: the artifact predated large-manifest-parse, and it also predated the stable toolchain moving from 1.92.0 to 1.97.1 mid-session, which makes every number recorded before it incomparable regardless of workload. The refreshed file records rustc 1.97.1 and ronin_dirty=false. Ronin against C samurai across the catalog, medians in milliseconds: command evaluation 7.550 against 9.695, deep graph 7.008 against 5.232, wide no-op 8.837 against 9.084, path canonicalization 4.940 against 5.595, dependency-log load 2.870 against 2.630, clean-tree no-op 9.026 against 9.777, large-manifest parse 305.351 against 323.829, scheduler barrier 39.779 against 35.903. Ronin is ahead on five of eight including the two that this programme added because they were unrepresented — the up-to-date tree and the large manifest — and behind on deep-graph evaluation, dependency-log load and the scheduler barrier. Those three are now the honest remaining gaps and none has been investigated with the cycle-and-miss instrumentation that proved decisive for the size question; the deep-graph shape in particular is a 2,000-edge chain, which is a pointer-chasing pattern quite unlike anything else in the catalog."
